      <div type="clause" n="48.1a">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 48.1a</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 48.1a" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="571" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis enim a iusticia regis inplacitatus ad consilium exierit et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Hn_48-1a.lnote.oe.16"/> ad inculpacionem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="f" target="#Hn_48-1a.lnote.oe.f"/> non responderit, XX ma[n]ce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Hn_48-1a.lnote.oe.17"/> uel ouerseunesse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Hn_48-1a.lnote.oe.18"/> regis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="ff" target="#Hn_48-1a.lnote.oe.ff"/> culpa sit.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 571 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_48-1a.lnote.oe.f" n="f" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">571</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sofort auf die Klage</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">immediately upon the complaint</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_48-1a.lnote.oe.ff" n="ff" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">571</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 34, 3&lt;sup&gt;r&lt;/sup&gt;</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. 34, 3&lt;sup&gt;r&lt;/sup&gt;</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_48-1a.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">571</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_48-1a.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">571</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">marce <hi rend="italic">Hss. Edd.; verbessert aus</hi> 37, 2; mͣ <hi rend="italic">Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">marce MSS edd.; corrected from 37, 2; mͣ Sc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_48-1a.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">571</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-sum <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-sum Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_48-1a.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">323</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Rechtsgang 14b—17f; Ducange <hi rend="italic">s. v. consilium</hi>. Dem wegen Notzucht von Amts wegen Beklagten, der Rechtsbeistand erbittet, weigert diesen der Richter: <hi rend="italic">iura non patiuntur, quod habeatis consilium contra regem</hi>, und schickt <hi rend="italic">narratores</hi> fort (um 1300); Güterbock <hi rend="italic">Stud. z. Engl. Strafproz</hi>. 29. 39—<hi rend="italic">mancas uel auerseunes</hi>, dahinter über Linie <hi rend="italic">-sum</hi> wohl statt <hi rend="italic">-ssam</hi>—48, 1b <hi rend="italic">aliquis</hi>{30}—48, 1c <hi rend="italic">-ssit</hi>{23} Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Rechtsgang 14b—17f; Ducange <hi rend="italic">s. v. consilium</hi>. When a man accused of rape ex officio asks for legal counsel, the judge refuses it to him: <hi rend="italic">iura non patiuntur, quod habeatis consilium contra regem</hi>, and sends the <hi rend="italic">narratores</hi> away (c. 1300); Güterbock <hi rend="italic">Stud. z. Engl. Strafproz</hi>. 29. 39—<hi rend="italic">mancas uel auerseunes</hi>, followed above the line by <hi rend="italic">-sum</hi>, probably for <hi rend="italic">-ssam</hi>—48, 1b <hi rend="italic">aliquis</hi>{30}—48, 1c <hi rend="italic">-ssit</hi>{23} Rs</seg></note>
      </div>
